---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Container from '../../components/Container.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import TranslationNotice from '../../components/TranslationNotice.astro';

/* Английская редакция `/privacy`, построена 2026-08-26 (правка «Достроить
 * английскую версию сайта»). Источник содержания — канонический документ
 * `docs/legal/public/privacy.md`, редакция 1.3 от 2026-08-25: та же
 * редакция и та же дата, что на русской странице `/privacy`, просто с
 * полным набором из двенадцати разделов канонического текста, а не с
 * сокращённым изложением `pages/privacy.astro`. Обязательная оговорка о
 * приоритете (`TranslationNotice`) стоит сразу после заголовка. */
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy — wfeels"
      description="How personal data is processed and protected on wfeels.site."
      noindex={true}>
  <Container>
    <Section>
      <h1 class="t-h1">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <TranslationNotice ruHref="/privacy" />
      <Prose>
        <p><strong>Revision 1.3 of 25 August 2026.</strong></p>
        <p>
          Status: the edition in force for the scheme «primary database in
          the Russian Federation → full copy in a closed Telegram chat».
        </p>

        <h2>1. General provisions</h2>
        <p>
          1.1. This Policy sets out how personal data of visitors to
          <code>https://wfeels.site</code>, people who submit an enquiry, and
          clients are processed and protected.
        </p>
        <p>
          1.2. Data controller: Сабуров Даниил Денисович, a self-employed
          individual under the special tax regime «Professional Income Tax»,
          Tax ID <code>183700967882</code>, place of business — Saint
          Petersburg.
        </p>
        <p>
          1.3. Contact for requests, withdrawal of consent, and personal-data
          enquiries: <a href="mailto:i@dsaburov.ru">i@dsaburov.ru</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          1.4. This Policy applies only to processing carried out by the
          Controller. Third-party sites and services act under their own
          documents.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Processing principles</h2>
        <p>The Controller:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>processes data lawfully, in good faith, and only for purposes defined in advance;</li>
          <li>does not collect data that is excessive for those purposes;</li>
          <li>ensures accuracy and, where necessary, correction of data;</li>
          <li>does not merge databases created for incompatible purposes;</li>
          <li>keeps data no longer than the purposes of processing or the law require;</li>
          <li>takes legal, organisational and technical protective measures;</li>
          <li>destroys or anonymises data once its purpose is achieved, unless another lawful basis for retention exists.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Categories of data subjects and purposes</h2>
        <h3>3.1. Site visitors</h3>
        <p>
          Purposes: secure operation of the site, protecting the form from
          automated submissions, and rate limiting.
        </p>
        <p>
          Data: IP address, page URL, time of the request, technical request
          markers, how long the form took to fill in, and the value of the
          anti-spam field.
        </p>
        <p>
          Basis: the Controller's legitimate interest in the site's security,
          provided the visitor's rights do not prevail; for data included in
          a submitted enquiry, the subject's consent also applies.
        </p>

        <h3>3.2. People submitting an enquiry</h3>
        <p>
          Purposes: to receive and process the enquiry, contact the sender,
          clarify the task, prepare a proposal, and, where the sender
          initiates it, conclude a contract.
        </p>
        <p>Data:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>name or preferred form of address;</li>
          <li>a contact the sender enters themself: email or Telegram username;</li>
          <li>the selected service;</li>
          <li>a description of the task;</li>
          <li>the URL of the page the form was sent from;</li>
          <li>IP address and limited technical anti-spam data;</li>
          <li>date and time of submission;</li>
          <li>the version of the Policy and of the separate consent;</li>
          <li>the fact and method of confirming consent;</li>
          <li>business correspondence relating to the enquiry, once pre-contractual discussion has begun.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Basis: the subject's separate consent — for submitting the form;
          once negotiations begin, also actions taken at the subject's
          initiative aimed at concluding a contract. These bases are not
          merged with processing for site security.
        </p>

        <h3>3.3. Clients and client representatives</h3>
        <p>
          Purposes: concluding and performing a contract, settlements,
          issuing a self-employed tax receipt, acceptance of work, warranty
          fixes, claims handling, and defence of lawful rights.
        </p>
        <p>
          Data: full name, position and authority of the representative,
          contact details, the party's requisites, the Tax ID of a corporate
          or sole-trader client, contracts, specifications, correspondence,
          and details of payments, acceptance reports, remarks, deliverables
          and access granted.
        </p>
        <p>
          Basis for the client itself: concluding and performing the
          contract, complying with legal duties, and defending rights. For a
          representative or contact person who is not a party to the
          contract: the legitimate interest of the Controller and of the
          represented client in concluding and performing the contract,
          provided that person's rights and freedoms do not prevail; the
          client supplies the authority and the minimum necessary contact
          details.
        </p>

        <h3>3.4. Authors of testimonials and case-study participants</h3>
        <p>
          Purposes: publishing a testimonial, a name, a position, a company
          name, a logo, project imagery and agreed metrics in the portfolio.
        </p>
        <p>
          Basis: for a trade name, logo and non-personal materials —
          separate contractual permission from the rights holder; for the
          name, position, image, quote or testimonial of an identifiable
          individual — that person's own separate consent to the disclosure
          of personal data. One basis does not substitute for the other.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Data that should not be sent through the form</h2>
        <p>
          The form is not intended for passport data, banking details,
          health information, biometric data, criminal-record data,
          political or religious views, details of intimate life, or
          personal data of third parties. Do not enter such information in
          the free-text field. If it is genuinely required for a project,
          the parties agree a separate secure channel and legal basis in
          advance.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Operations and methods of processing</h2>
        <p>
          The Controller may collect, record, systematise, accumulate,
          store, clarify, retrieve, use, transfer to a party lawfully
          entrusted with processing, block, delete and destroy data.
        </p>
        <p>
          Processing is carried out by automated and mixed means. No
          decision producing legal consequences for the subject is made
          solely on the basis of automated processing.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Storage location and recipients</h2>
        <p>
          6.1. Primary recording, systematisation, accumulation, storage,
          clarification and retrieval of data belonging to citizens of the
          Russian Federation take place in an SQLite database on a RUVDS
          VPS in the RUcloud data centre at: Russian Federation, Moscow
          Region, Korolyov, Pionerskaya St., 4.
        </p>
        <p>
          6.2. Once the record has been successfully written to the
          Russian primary database, a full copy of the enquiry is sent via
          the Telegram Bot API to the Controller's private service chat. If
          the primary write fails, nothing is sent to Telegram. The
          delivery identifier and result are stored separately from the
          text of the enquiry. The bot deletes the Telegram copy after 23
          hours; the private chat itself additionally has an independent
          «1 day» Telegram auto-delete timer, so the standard retention
          period does not exceed 24 hours.
        </p>
        <p>
          6.3. The full content of an enquiry is not written to container
          or application logs. Logs contain only the data needed for
          diagnostics and security.
        </p>
        <p>
          6.4. The Controller does not receive or store card data. Payment
          is made by bank transfer or through a personal «Request Money»
          request in the T-Bank app; the payer confirms the transfer in
          their own bank's app or interface.
        </p>
        <p>
          6.5. VPS infrastructure is provided by OOO «МТ ФИНАНС» (trading
          as RUVDS), Tax ID <code>7706424050</code>, OGRN{' '}
          <code>1157746680332</code>, registered address: 127051, Moscow,
          Tsvetnoy Blvd, 26, bldg. 1, room 12. This is a provider of leased
          computing infrastructure. The application and the enquiry
          database are administered by the Controller. Access to the
          application and database is restricted by technical means and the
          Controller's own credentials.
        </p>
        <p>
          6.6. The Controller does not sell personal data and does not
          transfer it for someone else's advertising.
        </p>
        <p>
          6.7. Telegram is a foreign service with distributed infrastructure
          and group entities across several jurisdictions. Transferring a
          full copy of the enquiry is a cross-border transfer. Its purpose
          is delivery to the Controller, not advertising. Before submitting
          the form, the user is shown this information and separately
          confirms consent to delivery of a copy via Telegram. Telegram's
          own terms are published in its{' '}
          <a href="https://telegram.org/privacy" rel="noopener">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          6.8. When replying to the sender by email, correspondence related
          to the enquiry may be processed within Yandex's mail
          infrastructure. The user chooses email as their contact
          themselves; if they gave a Telegram username instead, the reply
          is sent to that Telegram contact.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Retention periods</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>an enquiry that did not result in a contract is kept for no more than 90 calendar days from the date the form was submitted; related pre-contractual correspondence — no more than 90 days after the last substantive contact;</li>
          <li>the IP address in the rate limiter is kept for no more than one hour;</li>
          <li>diagnostic logs do not contain the full text of an enquiry and are limited by automatic rotation: no more than three 10 MB files per container; they are removed on overwrite or on deletion of the corresponding container and its storage;</li>
          <li>evidence of consent is kept for no more than 1095 calendar days from the date the form was submitted, to the extent needed to prove lawfulness;</li>
          <li>a contract, specification, acceptance reports, and payment and tax documents are kept for the mandatory period of that document; where no specific period is set — no longer than is justified by performance and the defence of rights, usually three years after an obligation ends, extended for the duration of any dispute that has begun;</li>
          <li>correspondence is kept only to the extent it confirms material terms, performance, settlements, a claim, or the lawfulness of processing, and is deleted together with the corresponding file;</li>
          <li>temporary passwords, tokens, private keys and backup codes are not archived with the contract file: once access is handed over or ends, they are revoked or deleted without waiting for the general document-retention period;</li>
          <li>contractual permission for non-personal case-study materials remains in force for the period stated in it; personal data cleared for disclosure is processed until the separate consent ends or a request to stop is received;</li>
          <li>an agreed SQLite backup is created every 24 hours in a separate Docker volume on the same Russian VPS and kept for no more than seven days;</li>
          <li>RUVDS's optional external backup service is not connected and is not claimed as a separate external copy.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Where the law or a contract requires a different period, that
          period applies. Once it expires, data is destroyed or anonymised.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Cookies and local storage</h2>
        <p>
          As of this revision, the site does not use cookies, advertising
          analytics, or cross-site tracking systems. The chosen interface
          theme may be stored in the browser's <code>localStorage</code>
          under the key <code>theme</code>; this value is not sent to the
          Controller as part of an enquiry.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before analytics, advertising pixels, external CAPTCHA, or other
          tracking technologies are connected, this Policy and the consent
          interface will be revised.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Protective measures</h2>
        <p>
          The Controller documents an assessment of possible harm, current
          threats, the level of protection required, and the applicable set
          of measures. Measures in place include access control,
          authentication, TLS, secrets protection, software updates, keeping
          the full text of enquiries out of logs, event logging, incident
          response, and agreed SQLite backups. Access is not published or
          shared with anyone who does not need it for their work. Before
          going live, a test-restore procedure from a local backup is
          carried out and recorded.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Rights of the data subject</h2>
        <p>
          A data subject may request information about processing, demand
          correction, blocking or deletion of data, withdraw consent,
          object to processing based on legitimate interest, and appeal the
          Controller's actions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Requests are sent to <a href="mailto:i@dsaburov.ru">i@dsaburov.ru</a>.
          To protect the data, the Controller may ask for information
          confirming the requester's identity and their connection to the
          data requested. No excessive documents are requested in response.
        </p>
        <p>
          Withdrawing consent does not make processing carried out before
          the withdrawal was received unlawful, and does not end processing
          for which another lawful basis exists after withdrawal.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Changes to this Policy</h2>
        <p>
          A new revision is published at the same address with a new number
          and date. Changes are not applied retroactively to consent
          already given. If a new purpose requires consent, it is requested
          separately before that processing begins.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Contacts</h2>
        <p>
          Сабуров Даниил Денисович<br />
          Tax ID: <code>183700967882</code><br />
          Tax status: Professional Income Tax payer, not a sole trader<br />
          Place of business: Saint Petersburg<br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:i@dsaburov.ru">i@dsaburov.ru</a>
        </p>
      </Prose>
      <a href="/en#contact" class="back-to-form">
        <span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Back to the form
      </a>
    </Section>
  </Container>
</Base>
